// The Shield of the Ancients, restored: look() for shape 828.
//
// WHY THIS CLASS REPLACES RETAIL AORTA (0x033C). The engine picks the
// usecode class for an item's events from its SHAPE NUMBER (item.cpp:1516,
// `uint32 class_id = _shape`), and the restored shield is shape 828,
// "Zealan ceremonial shield" (Douglas, 2026-10-08). Retail already has a
// class at 828, named AORTA, whose only event is a look() barking
// "Zealan ceremonial shield ". This file is declared under that name, so
// build_eusecode.py REPLACEs 0x033C rather than pinning a new id (a pin on
// a retail id is refused). No retail class calls into 0x033C at a fixed
// offset (a scan of every 0x11 call / 0x57 spawn operand in
// shared/data/USECODE.FLX, 2026-10-08), so the replacement disturbs nothing
// but this look().
//
// WHY NOT THE TypeAOFrizbee CLASS. ZEALSHLD.UNK's look() has the 1994 text
// for the restored shield on its frame-2 branch, but that class (1260) is
// reached only through npcnum 236, which the Map 17 halves carry and a
// create()d item does not (U8 has no setNpcNum intrinsic). The restored
// shield never reached it even when it was 539 frame 2: it dispatched
// retail SHIELD and said "shield".
//
// QUALITY 83 IS THE RESTORED SHIELD. Retail Pagan places two 828s of its
// own (U8SAVE.000 NONFIXED, Map 8 and Map 54; retail ANCTONES 0x048B
// searches for one), and EZREKAL.UNK's forgery speech is about exactly that
// copy: "the same shape it is and the wrong symbols it has ... I found it in
// the Temple in Pagan." So 828 alone does not identify the Shield of the
// Ancients. lv-patched/SHADES.UNK creates it and then `setQ(83)`s it,
// continuing the halves' 81/82. 828 is SF_GENERIC, which the getQuality/
// setQuality intrinsics ignore, so the read and the write both use the
// unconditional getQ/setQ (0x19/0x1A). Pagan's copies carry quality 0 and
// keep their retail text.
//
// The text is ZEALSHLD.UNK:15's, the 1994 name, kept as written
// ("Ancients Ones" included).
//
// KEPT FOR SAVE COMPATIBILITY since 2026-10-17. The restored Shield is now
// shape 879 (TypeSacredShield, the 1994 art; its look() is class 879,
// lv-new/SACSHLD.UNK), and SHADES no longer creates an 828 q83. But a save
// made before that day, between the Sacred Circle ceremony and the temple
// altar, still holds the Shield as 828 quality 83, and AOSCENE's altar
// still accepts it (its legacy TypeAOArtifact search). This class keeps
// that item's 1994 name. Pagan's quality-0 828s keep the retail text.

uses "item";

typeclass Aorta inherits Item
{
	process look();
}

process Aorta::look()
{
	if getQ() = 83
	{
		bark("Ceremonial Shield of the Ancients Ones");
		return;
	}

	bark("Zealan ceremonial shield ");
}
